From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: UIElement and FrameworkElement -- the element and layout

Every XAML element is a UIElement and FrameworkElement; there was none. Layout is the documented two-pass model: Measure (DesiredSize, margin included) and Arrange (RenderSize, offset in the parent) around the element's MeasureOverride/ArrangeOverride -- our classes' own, or an application's when it derives the element (it overrides IFrameworkElementOverrides on its outer object) -- with Width/Height, Min/Max, Margin, the alignments and Visibility; InvalidateMeasure/InvalidateArrange/UpdateLayout; the layout properties registered in the property system (their change re-measures). The many interfaces (IUIElement has 102 slots) are generated by make_ifaces.py from ifaces.txt -- interface identity (IIDs; per slot the method and its arguments' stack size on i386) per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), the overridable methods' names per the public API documentation -- with a stub per slot (E_NOTIMPL; an event's handler accepted), and our classes fill the slots they implement. Enums and XAML structs are boxed as IReference<T> (value.c), as programs unbox them. The implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
